वि-√ श्रथ् (only 3. sg. pf. Ā. -शश्रथे), to open for one's self, RV. ix, 70, 2 :
Caus. -श्रथयति (2. sg. Impv. -श्रथाय, Subj. aor. -शिश्रथः), to loosen, untie, RV.; AV.;
to remit, pardon (a sin), RV. iv, 12, 4;
to destroy, ib. ii, 28, 7.

वि-√ श्रम् P. -श्राम्यति (ep. also श्रमति, ˚ते; ind.p. श्रा॑म्य, or -श्रम्य),
to rest, repose, recreate one's self, ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to rest from labour, cease, stop, desist, Kāv.; Kathās.; Rājat.;
to rest or depend on (loc.), Kāv.;
to rest i.e. trust or confide in, rely on R.; Cāṇ.;
to feel at ease or comfortable, R.; Bhaṭṭ. :
Pass. -श्राम्यते or -श्रम्यते (aor. व्य्-अश्रामि or व्य्-अश्रमि, Vop.; esp. 3. sg. Impv.; -श्राम्यताम् or -श्रम्यताम्, ‘you may rest’, ‘enough of this’), Bhartṛ.; Ratnāv. :
Caus. -श्रामयति or -श्रमयति, to cause to rest, make to cease, stop, ŚāṅkhGṛ.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to cause to rest or settle down on (loc.), Ragh. :
Desid. See वि-शिश्रमिषु.

वि-√ श्रम्भ् (accord. to some, more correctly -स्रम्भ्) Ā. -श्रम्भते, to confide, be confident, trust in or rely on (loc.), BhP. (ind.p. -श्रभ्य = trustfully, with confidence) :
Caus. -श्रम्भयति, to relax, loosen, untie, Lāṭy.;
to inspire with confidence, encourage, MBh.

वि-√ श्रि P. Ā. -श्रयति, ˚ते, to set or put asunder, separate, throw open, open, RV.;
 (mostly Ā.) to go asunder, be opened or separated or expanded or spread or diffused, ib.;
to have recourse to, rely on W.

वि-√ 1. श्रु P. -शृणोति, to hear distinctly, TUp.; Hariv.; BhP. :
Pass. -श्रूयते (Ved. also Ā. -शृणुते), to be heard or be heard of far and wide, become known or famous, RV.; TBr.; MBh. &c.:
Caus. -श्रावयति, to cause to be heard everywhere, narrate, communicate, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to mention (one's name), MBh.;
to tell (with acc. of pers. and acc. [v.l. loc.] of thing), ib.;
to make famous, R.; Hariv.;
to cause to resound, MBh.

वि-√ स्रु P. -स्रवति, to flow forth or away, issue from (abl.), ŚBr.; MBh.;
to discharge or emit (any fluid), MBh.; R.;
to flow asunder (fig.), melt, dissolve, come to nothing, MBh. :
Caus. -स्रावयति, to cause to flow forth or away, MBh.;
to wash away, Car.;
to let blood (with gen. or acc. of pers.), Suśr.
